  "note": "One entry per NEFF SHAPE, which is the mini batch: a NEFF's leading dimension is FIXED, so every mini-batch size in the grid is a separate compile and a cell can only run a shape that exists. `source` is `compiled` when this lane built it and `s3-cache` when an earlier lane did -- a NEFF is a pure function of the seeded architecture, the target parameter count and the batch size, so reusing one is reusing the same bytes, which the SHA-256 records. `load_proof_seconds` is a 20 s trickle of exactly `mini_batch` rows served by a FRESH server, so a NEFF that loads but cannot serve is found here rather than inside a cell's warm-up."
